               <physDesc>
                  <objectDesc form="codex">
                     <supportDesc>
                        <support>parchment</support>
                        <extent>ff. 161 <dimensions type="leaf" unit="mm">
                              <height>225</height>
                              <width>155</width>
                           </dimensions>
                        </extent>
                        <condition><locus>Ff. 1-8</locus> have sustained soem minor damage, which
                           has resulted in some loss of text; the damaged areas have been repaired
                           using patches of paper.The lower half of <locus>f. 129</locus> has been
                           cut off. </condition>
                     </supportDesc>
                  </objectDesc>
                  <handDesc>
                     <summary>Ashkenazic semi-cursive script</summary>
                     <handNote><p>The scribe copied this for his personal use (colophon on <locus>f.
                              157r</locus>.</p>
                        <p>The original folios between <locus>ff. 67 and 75</locus> appear to have
                           been damaged or lost within a century after the completion of the
                           manuscript; the missing text was subsequently supplied (in a separate
                           quire) by a late-fourteenth-century or early-fifteenth-century Ashkenazic
                           hand.</p></handNote>
                  </handDesc>

